      "summary": "Devon and Cornwall Police’s account of Tess’s death, and their conclusion.",
      "detail": "Devon and Cornwall Police — summary for the family of the deceased, given to Mrs R. Rendle by the coroner’s officer.\n\nSaturday 18 November 2023\n08:42 — 999 call from Daniel KELLOW (café owner): woman unresponsive in a camper van, Marram Point car park, Croyde.\n08:52 — Ambulance arrives. Deceased (Tess RENDLE, 31) pronounced dead at the scene. Diesel night heater still running. Carbon monoxide poisoning (carboxyhaemoglobin 64% on initial post-mortem blood test; full toxicology awaited). Estimated time of death 01:00–03:00.\nVehicle: VW Transporter camper ‘Moss’, owner Callum RENDLE (brother), converted by his firm, Saltworks Vans, Braunton. Borrowed by the deceased on Friday 17 November.\nUnder the windscreen wiper, a note in block capitals: ‘NO OVERNIGHT SLEEPING. LAST WARNING. NEXT TIME I WON’T BE SO POLITE.’ Author not identified; similar notes are often left on vehicles at that car park.\n\nMonday 20 November — vehicle examination at the police compound, Barnstaple: heater exhaust joint not sealed. No gasket present; clamp loose, with tool marks indicating recent adjustment. Exhaust gases escaping into the seat box and the living area. CO alarm present, batteries fitted, functional on test (test button); why it did not activate is unclear — possibly sited too far from the heater. Engine and cooling system: no faults found.\n\nTuesday 21 November — Mr C. RENDLE interviewed voluntarily under caution regarding the installation. Vehicle retained at the police compound pending the inquest.\n\nNo suspicion of deliberate harm. Enquiries continue into the installation. File passed to the coroner; Trading Standards informed regarding Saltworks Vans."
